      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MR JONES (1) is the clear horse to beat after finishing second in a BM76 here, beaten a length after beginning slowly. He now finds easier, has a strong track-and-trip profile and the apprentice claim plus blinkers give him several positives despite the two-month break. SHEER REWARD (7) has only been fair in two 3yo+ BM48+ runs at Kununurra, but he returns to a more suitable 1600m setup and his previous win at this track and distance keeps him right in the race. OKESUTORA (3) has to turn around a plain Kununurra sixth, yet the nose defeat two starts back showed he is close enough when able to produce his best. Each-way. VALLEY PRINCE (6) was a solid BM64 third here after a poor run, and his broad 1600m record says he can be competitive.",
